### Some basic terms in time and space complexity

Time => How much time your program takes
Space complexity => How much extra space your algorithm takes.
Trade off=> Faster algorithm often uses more memory. Memory efficient algorithm may run slower
General rule=> More space -> Faster Execution . Less Space -> Slower excection
**Speed=>**How fast performace grows an input size increases . How performance scales when data becomes large .

**Time Complexity =>. Means Execution Steps **

**Space Complexity => Means Extra Memory Used **

Best , Worst and Average Case

Best Case
Algorithm work as fast as possible
Happens only for ideal case



**Worst Case **

Algorithm work as slow as possible
Cannot get worse than this
This is what interview focus on




**Average Case**
Performace on typical inputs
Harder to calculate
Often close to real world behaviour


Function Plays a important role in time and space complexity
A function is like a machine . It takes an input and produces an output
A function grows faster if its output increases more rapidly
Faster growth => Worse Scalability
n^2 = Grows faster
n^3 = Grow much faster





